{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"ca951f56d5b757d006c0d382323a799a8be2c4718dbef7899e11bd4bcf6f87c0","digest":{"component_or_area":"git index.lock retry mechanism and lifecycle tests","key_entities":["_with_index_lock_retry","_retry_probe","gitutil.py","test_compact_index_lock.py","test_delete_init_index_lock.py","_is_index_lock_error","_INDEX_LOCK_ATTEMPTS"],"problem_keywords":["index.lock contention","retry logic","test coverage","race condition","timing-dependent test"],"propositions":["Contended-lock tests use a 0.4s timer to unlink locks, but on slow runners the lock is removed before the first git attempt, bypassing the retry logic entirely.","The _with_index_lock_retry function's retry path is not exercised by current tests because the lock disappears before any index.lock error occurs.","A deterministic test seam (_retry_probe) is needed to synchronize lock release with confirmed first-attempt failure, replacing timer-based synchronization.","Non-index.lock git failures should return immediately after the first attempt and never enter the retry loop.","The retry probe must fire at every attempt (including the pre-loop initial call) and allow tests to inspect the result and control lock lifecycle without timing dependencies."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785823842918956713,"uuid":"70917c42-eb84-486f-948e-b76d761e1872"}